<h1>Talk</h1>

<h2>Description</h2>
<p>This research/artist talk follows work from coding GPU shaders to creating a new creative coding integrated development environment, to live coding music. Through performance and audience interaction, Char explores how the tools we use to create code fundamentally shape what we can imagine and express. Specifically, Char has been working on making the IDE (the software that we use to write software) into an expressive medium in its own right.</p>

<h2>Bio</h2>
<p>Char Stiles is a computational artist, educator, and programmer based in Brooklyn, NY. She works creatively in the lower levels of graphical computational systems and makes jokes about how computers work. She went to Carnegie Mellon University, where she earned a bachelor’s in fine art and computer science, and has a master’s in media arts and sciences from the MIT Media Lab. She is an associate professor in the Cooper Union computer science department. She co-founded Hex House, an artist studio and hacker space in East Williamsburg.</p>
